' including the other components' box labels as notes below.

class "L2 - Customer Order Processing / L3 Manage Customer Order Fulfillment\nL2 - Customer Order Processing / L3 Manage Customer Order Delivery" as OrderActivities <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class CustomerProductOrder <<SID Data Entity>>
class Product <<SID Data Entity>>

note right of CustomerProductOrder
  Drawn inside a separate component box
  labelled "TMFC002 - Product Order
  Capture & Validation" in the source image.
end note

note right of Product
  Drawn inside a separate component box
  labelled "TMFC005 - Product Inventory"
  in the source image.
end note

' Per the image's own legend, an arrow from the eTOM activity towards the SID
' ABE means information produced by the activity; the reverse arrow means
' information consumed by the activity. Both connections are drawn as a
' single line carrying an arrowhead at each end, i.e. both hold
' simultaneously -- confirmed by zooming into each arrowhead individually.
OrderActivities --> CustomerProductOrder : produces
CustomerProductOrder --> OrderActivities : is consumed by

OrderActivities --> Product : produces
Product --> OrderActivities : is consumed by

